;It rained 22% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"98.156875\" cy=\"302.375\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 32%&amp;#10;It rained 28% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"172.6261971830986\" cy=\"279.46478873239437\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 51%&amp;#10;It rained 52% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"239.25906249999997\" cy=\"194.3125\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 65%&amp;#10;It rained 45% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"289.63913043478266\" cy=\"218.46376811594203\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 77%&amp;#10;It rained 63% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 57 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"329.64842105263153\" cy=\"152.10526315789474\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 85%&amp;#10;It rained 69% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"360.20147058823534\" cy=\"130.41176470588235\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 92%&amp;#10;It rained 71% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"384.06794520547936\" cy=\"122.71232876712332\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 97%&amp;#10;It rained 61% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"400.6609375\" cy=\"160.1875\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 89% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 142 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.6011267605634\" cy=\"56.450704225352126\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(59%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In San Juan the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>summer</b> (0.20) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (-0.11).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>172</td><td class='num'>55%</td><td class='num'>-0.108</td><td class='num'>22.8%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>178</td><td class='num'>58%</td><td class='num'>0.100</td><td class='num'>13.9%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>144</td><td class='num'>66%</td><td class='num'>0.166</td><td class='num'>10.0%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>178</td><td class='num'>60%</td><td class='num'>0.198</td><td class='num'>13.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":18.46633,"lon":-66.10572,"n":672,"n_cities":216,"name":"San Juan","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.22,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.1134375,"n":64,"obs":0.21875,"sig":true},{"hi":0.44200000000000017,"lo":0.22,"mean":0.3238028169014085,"n":71,"obs":0.28169014084507044,"sig":false},{"hi":0.59,"lo":0.44200000000000017,"mean":0.5120312499999999,"n":64,"obs":0.515625,"sig":false},{"hi":0.73,"lo":0.59,"mean":0.6543478260869566,"n":69,"obs":0.4492753623188406,"sig":true},{"hi":0.82,"lo":0.73,"mean":0.7673684210526315,"n":57,"obs":0.631578947368421,"sig":true},{"hi":0.9,"lo":0.82,"mean":0.8536764705882354,"n":68,"obs":0.6911764705882353,"sig":true},{"hi":0.95,"lo":0.9,"mean":0.9210958904109586,"n":73,"obs":0.7123287671232876,"sig":true},{"hi":0.99,"lo":0.95,"mean":0.9679687499999999,"n":64,"obs":0.609375,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.99,"mean":0.9988732394366198,"n":142,"obs":0.8943661971830986,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":7.4,"provisional":false,"rank":183,"rank_hi":192.0,"rank_lo":157.0,"reliability":0.02908806939135333,"resolution":0.04813478899458358,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"san-juan","station":"LEVITTOWN 1.0 SE","timezone":"America/Puerto_Rico"}